CHANGED: Loading and normalization got faster, with unchanged output: GHC-to-Clash type conversion is memoized on the GHC type (halving the loading stage on large designs), transformation workers test their cheap disqualifying guards before computing type information, `liftBinding` prefilters its alpha-equivalence scan on a cached type fingerprint, the compile-time evaluator no longer recomputes free variables where it already tracks an in-scope set, and it only let-binds heap entries that the evaluated expression actually references.
